# Changelog

Every git commit that changes the project must update `CHANGELOG.md` in the same commit.

- Add the entry under `## [Unreleased]`.
- Use `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Fixed`, `### Removed`, or `### Security`.
- Write one English bullet for what changed and why. Do not skip a commit because it is small, a version bump, CI, or docs.
- When a release version is bumped, move the `Unreleased` notes into `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, add the release compare link, and leave `Unreleased` empty.
- Do not create the commit unless the user asked for it.

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Fixed

- Restored native paste in text fields. The app menu had replaced the system Edit menu.
```
